          <div><dt>What I did</dt><dd>Kubernetes and Helm releases that run the same on Azure and on offline servers, plus on-site work to fix network and deployment issues.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Result</dt><dd class="res">Regular releases reaching cloud and offline environments alike, and secure team access without extra VMs.</dd></div></dl>
          <ul class="tags"><li>Kubernetes</li><li>Helm</li><li>Azure</li><li>Air-gapped</li></ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card case rv">
          <span class="kick">MedSoft · Medical</span>
          <h3>Surgery, simulated in C++</h3>
          <dl><div><dt>Problem</dt><dd>Surgeons needed to plan orthognathic surgery and produce patient-specific hardware before entering the operating room.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What I did</dt><dd>Six C++/VTK/Qt plugins covering each procedure step, including a reusable screw placement widget shared across plugins.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Result</dt><dd class="res">FDA-approved software, now owned by Johnson &amp; Johnson. The widget cut about 20% of dev time in later sprints.</dd></div></dl>
          <ul class="tags"><li>C++17</li><li>VTK</li><li>Qt/QML</li><li>FDA</li></ul>
        </article>
        <article class="card case rv">
          <span class="kick">Archrete · Real-time 3D</span>
          <h3>Walk through it before it's built</h3>
          <dl><div><dt>Problem</dt><dd>Major architectural projects needed real-time, interactive presentations of buildings that did not exist yet.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>What I did</dt><dd>Unreal Engine 5 plugins in C++, exposed as Blueprints so artists could extend the simulations themselves.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Result</dt><dd class="res">iMaket simulations for large-scale developments, with blockers solved at the engine level.</dd></div></dl>
          <ul class="tags"><li>Unreal Engine 5</li><li>C++</li><li>Blueprints</li></ul>
        </article>
